                        ],
                        "form": "Juliuses"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4230b39b-7fcf-49ef-91ad-417ada51022b",
                        "entry_id": "92382689-0e0f-33fb-936c-9bfa4229c432",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Julii"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                        "entry_id": "92382689-0e0f-33fb-936c-9bfa4229c432",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A male given name from Latin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9dbc5ee-00f8-43bd-8bab-d9a6c09bb30e",
                                "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                                "text": "“Julius is Marguerite’s dog,” Jeanne Louise explained to Paul as she smiled at her Italian cousin. / “I thought Julius was Marguerite’s life mate?” Paul said with confusion. / “He is. There are two Juliuses,” Christian said with amusement. “One is a dog, and one is my father.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ae49493-fd2a-4b0a-92bf-306670276b45",
                                "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                                "text": "WHẽ it was cõcluded that we ſhulde ſayle into italy / they delivered Paul / and certayne other pꝛeſoners vnto won named Iulius / ã vnder captayne of Ceſars ſoudiars."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e284b1e8-d845-4537-b5ab-cb6eed1d94c4",
                                "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                                "text": "The seven [centurions] from II Adiutrix, whose stay in the province can be closely dated to the years 71–85/6, have an instructive set of names – two Julii, appropriately enough in a period when two of the governors also bore this name; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a92f0fa-b5bf-47fd-af10-28330abf372e",
                                "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                                "text": "Vespasian, a simple man, always laughed because so many Julii and Claudii were made divine after their deaths. On his deathbed he said, “Alas! I think I’m becoming a god.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d3969ef-6bd8-4e68-9b11-e76b7886115d",
                                "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                                "text": "So the man whom we know as Julius Caesar was a member of the Julii clan belonging to a particular branch whose paternal designation was Caesar. Only intimate family members would have called him Gaius. Caesar was known by his cognomen, presumably because there were many Julii and it would have caused confusion to use that nomen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fa4ca39-39f1-463d-a275-83435972b24a",
                                "sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
                                "text": "The other option for a coalition is the EFF, led by former ANC youth leader Julius Malema, who was expelled from the party more than a decade ago."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c3606ec-7c66-4ef9-868d-a6f1e66b9eb5",
                        "source_entry_id": "92382689-0e0f-33fb-936c-9bfa4229c432",
                        "source_sense_id": "f4fd63ac-de6f-30e5-a687-2951e3b7bcfa",
